{"title":"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A theatre has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/a/caa9bc3e1ca566d171ec6b80e39ee4cc913b5aa1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$600$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> seats. Exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/6/96633b73a86b9d9110e1ff824fce08def96ca296.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> of these seats are filled. All of the people in the seats then move to an empty theatre that has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/3/8f37626d49b4082c9102bf930bca51277ff2eb43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> seats. What percentage of the seats in the smaller theatre are now filled?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/9/84986317af8dcaee5ee14cf9008abc6941438e9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 50\\% \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 40\\% \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 60\\% \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 75\\% \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 55\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"509\" height=\"19\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>From the percentage and the fact that the larger theatre has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/a/caa9bc3e1ca566d171ec6b80e39ee4cc913b5aa1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$600$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> seats, we see that the number of people that were in seats was \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/c/2cc5f4d33f1f0bfbb1ef327cb571671c4a457b8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$600 \\times 25\\% = 600 \\times \\frac{1}{4} = 150$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"223\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>This would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/8/758886acf3a6693aa60a4bc243ed508ba3884ba2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{150}{200} = \\frac{3}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"70\" height=\"38\" /> of the seats in the smaller theatre, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/0/3507e9e02b9e980f0340ad3f50b4f0c6e4fe7470.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(D) } 75\\%}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"82\" height=\"31\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Because the larger theatre has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/a/d0a70b979a2160c312dbbc638b3bcdabd742b2c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{600}{200} = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"66\" height=\"38\" /> times the number of seats compared , the percentage of filled seats in the smaller theatre after everyone moves over there is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times the percentage of filled seats in the larger theatre before they moved.\n</p><p>Thus, the smaller theatre is now <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/8/c788d47345d0669904779936060e684d00347920.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25\\% \\times 3 = \\boxed {\\textbf {(D) } 75\\%}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"171\" height=\"31\" /> full.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley\">2025 CEMC Cayley</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"